1
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:06,800
Falling down a bottomless pit is boring
'cause it's taking SO LONG!

2
00:00:06,864 --> 00:00:08,976
Blocky, I see the bottom of this pit.

3
00:00:09,312 --> 00:00:11,360
"Bottomless" is such a lie.

4
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:11,856
A lie?

5
00:00:11,856 --> 00:00:13,552
What? There's a bottom?

6
00:00:13,552 --> 00:00:15,760
Oh, my tree, I see spikes!

7
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:20,720
AAAAAAAAA!

8
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:24,000
Need some money fast and soon?

9
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,024
Then buy our Box of Paper Slips!

10
00:00:27,440 --> 00:00:31,376
At first it might just seem like a blank slip of paper,

11
00:00:31,376 --> 00:00:34,752
but you can scribble a number on it, and POOF!

12
00:00:34,752 --> 00:00:36,432
It's a dollar bill!

13
00:00:36,432 --> 00:00:38,848
This person managed to buy a TV.

14
00:00:38,848 --> 00:00:40,840
This person bought a house!

15
00:00:40,840 --> 00:00:43,472
This person bought the world!

16
00:00:43,536 --> 00:00:46,224
So, yeah! BUY NOW!

17
00:00:46,512 --> 00:00:49,328
AAAAAAAAAAAAAA!

18
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:50,240
Huh?

19
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:51,728
Hey, it's Spongy!

20
00:00:52,064 --> 00:00:53,040
AAAAAA!

21
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:54,448
SPONGY:
Bueeuuugh-OOO!!

22
00:00:54,448 --> 00:00:56,832
AAAAAAAAA!

23
00:00:58,928 --> 00:01:00,416
Hey, it's you!

24
00:01:00,416 --> 00:01:05,648
Yes, it's me. And I have to tell you that your team,
the SquAHshy Grapes, lost last episode's contest.

25
00:01:05,904 --> 00:01:07,744
Go that way to the Cake at Stake place.

26
00:01:07,744 --> 00:01:10,704
Walk! Run! Jog! Walk! Run! Jog! Walk! Run! Jog! Walk! Run! Jog!

27
00:01:10,832 --> 00:01:17,584
♪ [INTRO PLAYS] ♪

28
00:01:17,584 --> 00:01:19,580
Subtitles: Daniel Adam Valle

29
00:01:19,936 --> 00:01:24,336
I am so glad to see that we're no longer the losers!

30
00:01:24,336 --> 00:01:28,562
Yeah, well, Bubble, you almost made us lose.

31
00:01:28,562 --> 00:01:30,352
So don't do that again.

32
00:01:30,608 --> 00:01:31,776
We're getting close.

33
00:01:31,776 --> 00:01:32,560
Halt.

34
00:01:32,560 --> 00:01:34,880
Since this is a new stage in
the Battle for Dream Island,

35
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:37,072
we need to renovate the Cake at Stake place.

36
00:01:37,168 --> 00:01:38,544
[TA-DA!]

37
00:01:38,544 --> 00:01:41,344
That's all you can afford to do?

38
00:01:41,344 --> 00:01:42,192
No. There's more.

39
00:01:42,192 --> 00:01:43,376
[TA-DA!]

40
00:01:43,376 --> 00:01:49,040
Wow! Ooh! Wow! Ooh, wooow, that's amazing!
Oh, my gosh! That's amazing! Woooah!

41
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,192
So, yeah, sit.

42
00:01:50,192 --> 00:01:51,984
Squashy!

43
00:01:52,320 --> 00:01:53,936
♪ Hork hork hork, glorp glorp ♪

44
00:01:53,936 --> 00:01:55,616
♪ Gloop gloop gloop, doot doot ♪

45
00:01:55,616 --> 00:01:56,848
♪ Cake at Stake! ♪

46
00:01:56,848 --> 00:01:58,912
This time, we got twenty-nine votes.

47
00:01:58,912 --> 00:02:03,680
As you know, the three of you with the fewest votes
receive a slice of cake, and will stay in the game.

48
00:02:04,128 --> 00:02:05,696
The other two will leave the team.

49
00:02:06,016 --> 00:02:08,912
However, the winning team will choose
one of the two onto their team.

50
00:02:08,912 --> 00:02:09,760
Let's start.

51
00:02:09,968 --> 00:02:11,968
Blocky, do you want to use your Win Token?

52
00:02:11,968 --> 00:02:15,664
No! I just got this thingy last episode!

53
00:02:15,664 --> 00:02:16,784
Ok, then.

54
00:02:16,992 --> 00:02:19,200
At the lowest, with one vote, is Ice Cube.

55
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:20,064
Wha?

56
00:02:20,112 --> 00:02:22,320
Hey! That's not cake!

57
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:24,032
That's modeling clay!

58
00:02:24,032 --> 00:02:25,648
The cake was too expensive.

59
00:02:25,728 --> 00:02:27,640
Blocky, you're safe at two votes.

60
00:02:28,208 --> 00:02:29,056
Yeah!

61
00:02:29,536 --> 00:02:31,744
ANNOUNCER:
Leafy, Teardrop, and Snowball,

62
00:02:31,984 --> 00:02:33,520
only one of you is safe.

63
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:36,368
and that person happens
to be Leafy, with three votes.

64
00:02:36,592 --> 00:02:38,096
Yes! Whaaa?

65
00:02:38,096 --> 00:02:39,616
ANNOUNCER:
Teardrop and Snowball...

66
00:02:39,616 --> 00:02:42,512
you got five and eighteen votes respectively.

67
00:02:43,040 --> 00:02:43,728
Come with me.

68
00:02:44,464 --> 00:02:47,680
Well, guys, we may be a little smaller,

69
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:50,320
but we're still the best team ever!

70
00:02:52,704 --> 00:02:54,144
ANNOUNCER:
Snowball and Teardrop,

71
00:02:54,144 --> 00:02:57,648
the Squishy Cherries will either vote
you onto their team or to be eliminated.

72
00:02:57,872 --> 00:02:59,200
So Eraser, please pick.

73
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:02,080
I want Snowball on my team!

74
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:04,608
He's just AWESOME!

75
00:03:05,504 --> 00:03:08,304
Well, Snowball's not so smart,

76
00:03:08,304 --> 00:03:09,968
so I'll say Teardrop!

77
00:03:10,608 --> 00:03:13,728
OMG, I so totally, like, agree.

78
00:03:13,728 --> 00:03:17,184
I choose Teardrop. SB is totally a jerk.

79
00:03:17,792 --> 00:03:20,768
No, I think SB is...

80
00:03:20,768 --> 00:03:22,672
is AWESOME!

81
00:03:23,664 --> 00:03:26,048
Oh, so it's all down to me.

82
00:03:26,944 --> 00:03:28,464
Uhhhgh...

83
00:03:28,672 --> 00:03:30,128
Uh, well...

84
00:03:30,640 --> 00:03:33,936
Snowball won contests four and five, so I pick him.

85
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:36,928
Teardrop, it's time to say goodbye.

86
00:03:39,168 --> 00:03:41,824
Yeah! Still in it to WIN IT!

87
00:03:41,856 --> 00:03:43,820
So now it is down to the final fourteen.

88
00:03:45,376 --> 00:03:47,392
The tenth contest is a crying contest.

89
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:49,824
Fill your tubs as high as you can with tears.

90
00:03:50,816 --> 00:03:53,520
Ehhh, EH! EH, EH!

91
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:54,192
EHH!!!

92
00:03:54,192 --> 00:03:56,896
Eraser, you're not crying!

93
00:03:56,896 --> 00:03:59,024
Crying is for WIMPS!

94
00:03:59,024 --> 00:04:01,296
Snowball? You, too!?

95
00:04:01,296 --> 00:04:05,760
WHY should I TRY to CRY?!

96
00:04:06,064 --> 00:04:07,744
Oh, no!

97
00:04:07,744 --> 00:04:08,256
HEUGH-

98
00:04:08,256 --> 00:04:09,776
CRYYYIIING!

99
00:04:09,776 --> 00:04:10,736
HEUUUGH-

100
00:04:11,024 --> 00:04:13,488
Oh, oh, no, OH,

101
00:04:13,488 --> 00:04:14,256
NOOO!!!

102
00:04:14,368 --> 00:04:15,840
Uh...so?

103
00:04:15,872 --> 00:04:17,648
Don't you know, Coiny?

104
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:19,824
Crying? Tears?

105
00:04:20,064 --> 00:04:22,144
Water is my POISON!

106
00:04:22,144 --> 00:04:23,888
Sorry! I forgot!

107
00:04:25,568 --> 00:04:26,512
Try to cry!

108
00:04:26,512 --> 00:04:27,632
Okay.

109
00:04:27,632 --> 00:04:29,312
EEEEEHHH!

110
00:04:29,312 --> 00:04:30,944
Not a drop! I'll try.

111
00:04:31,008 --> 00:04:33,040
ULEGEUGHAUGHEUAGLUGAUGALAGUHUAHGYGHAG!

112
00:04:34,272 --> 00:04:36,304
Yeah! Low five!

113
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:39,232
Hey, let's melt Icy!

114
00:04:39,376 --> 00:04:40,400
Heegh...HYUP!

115
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:41,072
Heh?

116
00:04:42,032 --> 00:04:44,112
[GASP] That was mean!

117
00:04:44,112 --> 00:04:45,744
That was MEAN!

118
00:04:45,744 --> 00:04:47,312
Boop. Time's up!

119
00:04:47,664 --> 00:04:50,000
Since you all got some water, I guess it's a tie.

120
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,216
No fair! Look how much water we ha-

121
00:04:53,216 --> 00:04:54,832
The tiebreaker is a skiing contest.

122
00:04:54,832 --> 00:04:56,272
Hey, Match, look!

123
00:04:56,272 --> 00:04:58,656
It's mini-Snowball!

124
00:04:58,656 --> 00:05:01,472
Ooh, I'll get my mini-Match.

125
00:05:01,472 --> 00:05:03,952
Let's play Spongy Cake!

126
00:05:03,952 --> 00:05:06,848
People, try to get to the finish ASAP.

127
00:05:06,848 --> 00:05:09,792
Oh, and we could only afford
one pair of skis for each team.

128
00:05:09,792 --> 00:05:10,560
What?

129
00:05:10,976 --> 00:05:11,440
Go.

130
00:05:11,728 --> 00:05:13,568
Oh, my gosh!

131
00:05:13,968 --> 00:05:14,736
Ready?

132
00:05:14,736 --> 00:05:16,560
Huh? Not quite...

133
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:19,136
I still don't like what you did to Icy.

134
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:24,112
Hey! The Ice Cube Recovery Center
will make Ice Cube alive again!

135
00:05:24,112 --> 00:05:25,280
Still!

136
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:28,496
- How's it going?
- Uh, wobbly!

137
00:05:28,496 --> 00:05:29,792
Hey, where's Rocky?

138
00:05:29,792 --> 00:05:30,560
There!

139
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,896
WEAAAAUUUUUGH!!!!

140
00:05:44,352 --> 00:05:46,880
Three, two, one, JUMP!

141
00:05:54,528 --> 00:05:56,224
Which is which?

142
00:05:56,224 --> 00:05:57,344
I don't know!

143
00:06:01,072 --> 00:06:02,176
Icy!

144
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:10,080
Well, it's pretty obvious that
Leafy and Blocky got second place,

145
00:06:10,160 --> 00:06:13,904
but I'm not sure which of the other two
teams were in first place or third place,

146
00:06:14,112 --> 00:06:15,696
so we need another tiebreaker.

147
00:06:15,696 --> 00:06:17,690
Aw, seriously?

148
00:06:17,744 --> 00:06:19,536
It is a handstand contest.

149
00:06:19,536 --> 00:06:21,760
When I press the button, the ropes will release

150
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:25,456
If you are the last one handstanding,
your team wins, and you get a Win Token.

151
00:06:25,456 --> 00:06:27,232
The other team is in dead last.

152
00:06:27,232 --> 00:06:27,792
Go.

153
00:06:30,928 --> 00:06:31,520
Bleh!

154
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:32,224
Ha-ha!

155
00:06:34,016 --> 00:06:35,840
Another Name has already lost.

156
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,896
The Cherries win again, but who will get the Win Token?

157
00:06:39,136 --> 00:06:39,984
Bleh!

158
00:06:39,984 --> 00:06:45,328
Whoooaaaa! Oh, oh, no! Oh, nooo! Whoaaa!
HEUUUGH! Habubabubabah! Heeuuugh oh, nooo!

159
00:06:45,328 --> 00:06:47,184
Huu! Huuu!! HUUU!! HUUUUU!

160
00:06:47,184 --> 00:06:49,180
HUU! HUUU! HUU! HUU!

161
00:06:49,180 --> 00:06:50,624
ANNOUNCER:
Eraser gets his second Win Token.

162
00:06:50,624 --> 00:06:51,216
YEAH!

163
00:06:51,216 --> 00:06:52,576
ANNOUNCER:
You can only use one at a time.

164
00:06:52,576 --> 00:06:53,424
AWH!

165
00:06:53,424 --> 00:06:55,536
ANNOUNCER:
The Cherries go to first, and the Names to last.

166
00:06:55,840 --> 00:06:59,632
Voters, choose one member of Another Name to leave BFDI.

167
00:06:59,824 --> 00:07:02,832
TB, GB, Rocky, Coiny or Firey.

168
00:07:03,104 --> 00:07:06,816
The two most voted will leave the team.
One will join the Cherries.

169
00:07:11,824 --> 00:07:14,816
Would you look at that? My very first tear!

170
00:07:15,040 --> 00:07:18,144
I'll always remember this for the rest of my life.